nsuring that the body can accept the transplanted tissue. Additionally, HLA is associated with the body's immune response and has implications for susceptibility to various conditions, including autoimmune diseases such as Type 1 Diabetes and allergies, particularly food allergies. The HLA system is characterized by a high frequency of genetic recombination, which is relevant in the context of genetic inheritance, including conditions like congenital adrenal hyperplasia. Overall, HLA is integral to both transplant medicine and the understanding of immune-related health issues.\",7\r\n527,TUMORES,\"TUMORES refer to abnormal growths of cells that can be either benign or malignant. They are associated with various medical conditions and complications. For instance, gastric or colon tumors may indicate the need for parenteral nutrition, particularly in patients suffering from malnutrition. Additionally, tumors can lead to hypopituitarism, which affects hormone production in the pituitary gland. They are also a significant consideration in patients presenting with dysphagia, as tumors can impair esophageal function. Furthermore, tumors can be a contributing factor to the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), especially in cases involving pulmonary and non-thoracic tumors. In some instances, tumors may necessitate a hematopoietic cell transplant due to their impact on the body’s cellular functions.\",6\r\n2319,EICH,\"EICH, or Graft-versus-Host Disease (GVHD), is a significant complication that can arise following hematopoietic cell transplantation, including stem cell transplants. This condition manifests in both acute and chronic forms and occurs when the transplanted immune cells (the graft) attack the recipient's (the host's) tissues. EICH can lead to various health issues, affecting the patient's metabolism and overall well-being.\n\nPatients experiencing EICH may require specific dietary considerations, particularly those undergoing treatments such as hematopoietic cell transplants. The condition can be influenced by factors such as mucositis and the administration of glutamine treatment. It is crucial for healthcare providers to monitor and manage the nutritional needs of patients with EICH to support their recovery and mitigate complications.\n\nIn summary, EICH is a serious complication of hematopoietic stem cell transplantation that necessitates careful attention to both medical and nutritional management to enhance patient outcomes.\",15\r\n13741,ALOGÉNICO,\"Alogénico refers to a type of bone marrow transplantation in which the donor is a different individual, as opposed to an autologous transplant where the donor and recipient are the same person. This procedure often necessitates additional nutritional support for the recipient. The alogénico transplant involves the use of compatible donor cells to treat both malignant and non-malignant diseases.\",4\r\n2315,TPH,\"TPH refers to hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, a medical procedure involving high doses of chemotherapy followed by the infusion of hematopoietic cells.\",11\r\n2320,EVOH,\"EVOH, which stands for hepatic veno-occlusive disease, is a complication that can arise following hematopoietic stem cell transplantation. This condition, known in Spanish as \"\"Enfermedad Vascular Obstructiva del Hígado,\"\" can also affect transplant patients and necessitates appropriate nutritional management.\",2\r\n13786,TRANSPLANTE HEMATOLÓGICO,\"El trasplante hematológico es un procedimiento médico en el que se transfieren células madre hematopoyéticas a un paciente para tratar diversas enfermedades, incluyendo cáncer y trastornos de la sangre.\",2\r\n13824,CITOKINAS INFLAMATORIAS,Cytokines are inflammatory substances that can be elevated in patients undergoing treatment and may contribute to complications.,1\r\n13787,MUSCARITOLI ET AL,Muscaritoli et al son investigadores que han estudiado el impacto de la administración de lípidos en la incidencia